<title>USA: Lexmark sees 15 pct market share by 2000.</title>
<headline>Lexmark sees 15 pct market share by 2000.</headline>
<dateline>SAN FRANCISCO 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lexmark International Group Inc is confident it can reach its goal of capturing a 15 percent share of the worldwide market for inkjet and laser printers by 2000, a senior company executive said on Monday.</p>
<p>Lexmark currently holds about 10 percent of the market.</p>
<p>Bernard Masson, vice president and general manager of the consumer printer division, told Reuters after a presentation at the Robertson Stephens Tech '97 Agenda conference in San Francisco that the company had confidence that it could meet that target.</p>
</text>
